    "fullDescription": "The Electro-Surgical Skin Cautery Unit is a precision-engineered medical device designed for dermatological, cosmetic, and plastic surgical procedures. It delivers high-frequency monopolar and bipolar currents, enabling safe and effective coagulation, desiccation, and fulguration. The portable briefcase design ensures easy transport and safe storage, making it an ideal choice for clinics and hospitals alike.This unit is specially crafted to handle a wide range of minor surgical applications such as the removal of skin tags, warts, corns, cysts, and small tumors. It also supports advanced procedures like collagen remodeling, non-ablative skin treatments, epilation, nipple and forehead lifts, and hair restoration surgeries.Thanks to its accurate intensity control (50–100W), user-friendly interface, and exceptional safety features, this cautery device delivers excellent cosmetic results with minimal side effects and quicker patient recovery. Perfect for dermatologists, E.N.T specialists, plastic surgeons, general surgeons, and cosmetologists. Applications\t\tDermatology &amp; Cosmetic Treatments\t\t\tSkin tag, wart, cyst &amp; lesion removal\t\t\tHair restoration &amp; facial lifts\t\t\tCollagen remodeling and epilation\t\t\tPlastic and reconstructive surgeries\t\t\tTumor and keloid ablation\t\t\tPalatoplasty, blepharoplasty, mamoplasty\t\t\tMinor biopsies and abdominoplasty\t\t\tENT &amp; oral surgeries (tongue lesion, epistaxis, etc.)\t\t\tSkin flap development and aesthetic procedures\t Special Features\t\tMonopolar &amp; bipolar current options\t\t\tCompact briefcase design for portability\t\t\tPrecision-controlled intensity (50W–100W)\t\t\tIdeal for coagulation, desiccation, fulguration\t\t\tSafe for both invasive &amp; non-invasive skin procedures\t\t\tMinimal tissue damage, no charring, and quick healing\t\t\tExcellent cosmetic results with reduced downtime\t Technique OverviewThe unit operates using focused high-frequency waves that pass through interchangeable electrodes tailored for specific procedures. When activated, the waves heat intracellular water, converting it to steam, and gently dissolve tissue cells. The process ensures a clean, controlled incision or coagulation with minimal trauma. Output intensity can be finely tuned based on procedural depth and sensitivity, making it a superior alternative to conventional diathermy.",
